.TH CRUNCH_KEYCTL 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
crunch_keyctl \- Linux x86-64 syscall 250
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <sys/syscall_220_259.h>
.B long crunch_keyctl(int operation, unsigned long arg2, unsigned long arg3, unsigned long arg4, unsigned long arg5);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
Invokes raw keyctl with machine-word arguments. For pointer-valued arguments,
store the pointer in the pointer member of union crunch_syscall_word and pass
its value member. The union preserves the address bits on Linux x86-64.
This is a direct Linux x86-64 syscall wrapper; availability and permissions depend on the kernel and security policy.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the syscall result, or \-1 with errno set on failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR keyctl (2)
